  "articleBody": "Have you noticed your living room just isn't as functional or comfortable as it used to be? It's a common feeling as our needs or family situations change. Maybe movement through the room feels more difficult, or you're constantly tripping over rugs or furniture. Perhaps seating isn't as easy to get in and out of, or things you use regularly are just out of reach. Often, it comes down to how the space is laid out, the type of furniture, and even small details like flooring transitions and lighting. If your circulation paths feel constricted, or if it’s tough to navigate with a walker or a wheelchair, your living room isn’t serving you well. These issues can sneak up on you, making a once-loved space feel frustrating. Thinking about how you actually *use* the room and identifying those pinch points is the first step. HH Remodeling LLC can help you assess these challenges and come up with solutions to make your living room work for you again.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}